@kind(api)

@meta{
  crate: tomet-search
}

=[ tomet-search ]

Pure in-memory search and query engine for Tomet documents.

Provides:

- @strong[[`structural`]]: AST element query matching by tag, key, and value content.
- @strong[[`filter`]]: Document metadata query filtering and sorting over in-memory rows.

==[ Module filter ]

In-memory metadata query filtering and sorting engine.

Evaluates predicate expressions (e.g. `contains(meta.tags, "rust")`, `exists(meta.date)`)
and sort keys (e.g. `by(meta.date, "desc")`) across collections of metadata rows.

This engine performs no filesystem I/O: candidate rows are provided as in-memory
[`IndexRow`] structures.

===[ Structs ]

====[ struct IndexRow ]

One candidate document's queryable facts.

====[ struct IndexQueryError ]

An error encountered when parsing or executing an index query.

====[ struct SortKey ]

A sort key with its direction.

====[ struct Query ]

Parsed filter query consisting of an optional combined predicate and sort keys.

===[ Functions ]

====[ fn err ]

====[ fn is_index_document ]

Whether `doc` is an index document -- `@kind(doc.index)`, nothing else.

Not "does it contain a `${filter(...)}}`": an index document may be
entirely hand-written `@link(ref:"...")` entries with no query in it at
all, and that is still an index document. `@kind` is the one source of
truth; the filename is not consulted here either (a caller that wants a
cheap pre-parse filter, e.g. tomet-book's `.index.tmt` suffix, applies
it before ever calling this).

====[ fn known_paths ]

Collects every field path any row carries in `rows`.

====[ fn sort_key ]

Reads one `by(field)` / `by(field, "asc"|"desc")` argument.

====[ fn dotted_path ]

Converts an AST identifier or member chain into a dotted string path.

====[ fn unknown_fields ]

Finds field paths referenced in `predicate` that no row in `known` possesses.

====[ fn context_for ]

Builds an evaluation context with every known path bound, or `Null` if absent.

====[ fn sort_value ]

Reads the value for a sort key, treating `Null` as absent.

==[ Module structural ]

Structural AST query matching.

Provides pure in-memory querying over Tomet AST elements by tag,
attribute/property key, and value content.

===[ Structs ]

====[ struct StructuralQuery ]

Criteria for matching AST elements.

====[ struct StructuralMatch ]

A matched AST element occurrence with its span and tag name.

===[ Functions ]

====[ fn matches_query ]

Checks if a single element matches `query`.

====[ fn count_structural_matches ]

Counts matching elements in `doc` for `query`.

====[ fn find_structural_matches ]

Finds all matching element occurrences in `doc` for `query`.
